-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",69,{
[2177]="700452A5\n1\tFind the clearing where Théoden meets with his advisors\tThéoden meets with his advisors in a clearing at the base of Eilenach, in Taur Drúadan.\n2\tTalk to Théoden outside his tent in Taur Drúadan\030Talk to Éomer outside Théoden's tent in Taur Drúadan\tThéoden meets with his advisors in a clearing at the base of Eilenach, in Taur Drúadan.\n3\tTalk to Ghân-buri-Ghân while he meets with Théoden\tGhân-buri-Ghân is meeting with Théoden and his advisors in Taur Drúadan.\n4\tClear fallen stones near the northern entrance to Stonewain Valley\tThe entrance to the Stonewain Valley is far south of the Rohirrim encampment, and north-east of Drû Bhûta.\n5\tClear fallen stones in the Stonewain Valley\tThe Stonewain Valley runs north and south, not far from Drû Bhûta, in Taur Drúadan.\n6\tClear fallen stones in the Stonewain Valley\tThe Stonewain Valley runs north and south, not far from Drû Bhûta, in Taur Drúadan.\n7\tClear fallen stones in the Stonewain Valley\tThe Stonewain Valley runs north and south, not far from Drû Bhûta, in Taur Drúadan.\n8\tClear fallen stones in the Stonewain Valley\tThe Stonewain Valley runs north and south, not far from Drû Bhûta, in Taur Drúadan.\n9\tTalk to Éomer at the southern end of Stonewain Valley\tÉomer is at the southern end of the Stonewain Valley.\n",
[2178]="700001E6\n1\tEnter the Helegrod treasury and end the Nazgûl's schemes\tHelegrod is north of Rivendell and Glóin's camp. Elrond has asked you to enter the treasury of Helegrod and put a stop to the Nazgûl's schemes. He warned you to gather allies. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n2\tTalk to Elrond\tElrond can be found in the library of Imladris. In the treasury, you encountered the Nazgûl and were able to defeat him. You also interrupted the ritual being performed by the Gaunt-lord to restore the dragon Thorog, although part of the process was completed, and the dragon flew off. Elrond should be made aware of what happened.\n",
[2179]="700452A9\n1\tTalk to Éomer from horseback and join Théoden's Riders\tÉomer is at the southern end of the Stonewain Valley, and he prepares to ride out of the vale and toward the Pelennor's encircling wall.\n2\tTalk to Théoden on the Field of Onslaught\tThéoden's Riders have taken the field!\n",
[2180]="7002C5F1\n1\tDefeat gredbyg in the Rushgore (total: 3)\030Defeat avanc in the Rushgore (total: 3)\030Defeat turtles in the Rushgore (total: 3)\tEdbrit has asked you to defeat gredbyg, turtles, and avanc that have been stirred up in the Rushgore. Something has caused the creatures of the Rushgore to become more hostile than usual, and Edbrit wants you to help him deal with them before the two of you go in search of the falling shadow.\n2\tTalk to Edbrit\tEdbrit is at Aculf's Camp in the Rushgore. You have helped deal with some of the newly-aggressive creatures in the Rushgore, and should return now to Edbrit.\n3\tFind the location in the Brown Lands where the falling shadow came to earth\tEdbrit saw a mysterious shadow fall from the sky far to the south-east, in the Brown Lands. You have decided to travel to the Brown Lands in search of the mysterious shadow Edbrit saw.\n4\tTalk to Edbrit\tEdbrit is standing by the corpse of a mighty beast in the Brown Lands. You have found the body of a massive beast, and should speak to Edbrit about it.\n5\tTalk to Nona\tNona is standing by the corpse of the fallen beast in the Brown Lands. Nona is waiting to speak with you.\n",
[2181]="7002C697\n1\tComplete the deed 'The Vanished Rider' to learn the location of the missing Nazgûl\tThe great beast that crashed in the Brown Lands is missing its rider, but people throughout the lands bordering the Great River may have seen signs of it. You should seek them out and learn where the rider has gone.\n2\tTalk to Nona\tYou have scoured the lands near the Great River for some sign of the missing Nazgûl, but have always been half a step behind. You should meet with Nona back by the corpse of the crashed beast as you agreed.\n",
[2182]="7002C69C\n1\tTalk to Nona by the Carcass of the Beast and walk with her back to Stangard\tNona is standing by the carcass of the beast in the Brown Lands. Your search for the missing Nazgûl has proven fruitless, and Nona wants to walk with you back to Stangard where you can find more information.\n2\tTalk to Galadriel outside the House of Celeborn\tGaladriel is atop the flet on which is built the House of Celeborn, in Lothlórien. The night was long, but Galadriel has once again summoned you to speak with her.\n",
[2183]="700452AA\n1\tTalk to Prince Imrahil on the Field of Onslaught\tPrince Imrahil has led his swan-knights out of the city, and can be found on the Field of Onslaught. Théoden marked the emergence of the swan-knights from the city, and wants you to find Prince Imrahil.\n2\tFind an Orc that has broken free of the fighting ranks and defeat it\tGondorian soldiers and Rohirrim riders do battle with the Orcs on the Field of Onslaught. You should slay any of the Orcs that break free of the fighting ranks.\n3\tDefeat Orcs on the Pelennor during the battle (total: 6)\tGondorian soldiers and Rohirrim riders do battle with the Orcs on the Field of Onslaught. You should slay any of the Orcs that break free of the fighting ranks.\n4\tTalk to Déorwine at the fighting ranks to the south-east, on the Field of Onslaught\030Talk to Sakalbâr at the fighting ranks on the south-east side of the Field of Onslaught\tDéorwine and Sakalbâr are fighting on the south-eastern stretch of the line on the Field of Onslaught.\n5\tTalk to Fastred near the fighting ranks to the south-east on the Field of Onslaught\030Talk to Gimilkhôr near the fighting ranks to the south-east on the Field of Onslaught\tFastred and Gimilkhôr are near the south-eastern stretch of the line on the Field of Onslaught.\n6\tSearch for Crúmgam on the eastern side of the Field of Onslaught\tFastred has asked you to search the battlefield for his hated foe Crúmgam.\n7\tEncourage dismounted Rohirrim to fight (total: 3)\030Defeat your foes on the Pelennor during the battle (total: 8)\tRohirrim that have been dismounted from their steeds need your help on the eastern side of the Field of Onslaught.\n8\tReturn to Théoden on the Field of Onslaught\tThéoden is waiting with his banner-bearer, Guthláf, on the Field of Onslaught.\n",
[2184]="7001474E\n1\tTalk to Haldir upon a flet south-east of the river Nimrodel\tThere are wardens on the bounds of Lothlórien, east of Moria. Such Elves may be found on great platforms, or flets, among the trees to the south-east of the river Nimrodel. Bósi believes the dwarves cannot turn Mazog's Orcs aside for long if they are truly supported by some force out of Dol Guldur, and wants you to seek an audience with Galadriel of Lórien. The dwarves need allies if they are to stand in Khazad-dûm.\n",
[2185]="700001C3\n1\tTalk to Daervunn\tEsteldín lies in the North Downs, far to the north and west of Rivendell. Aragorn has asked you to travel to Esteldín in his stead to speak with Daervunn, whom he hopes can shed light on the troubling message.\n",
[2186]="7002BFA4\n1\tFind a bedroll in Grimbold's camp and get some rest\tA bedroll you can use is located south of Grimbold's position in his camp, by the milestone. Grimbold wants you to get some rest while you can.\n2\tTalk to Grimbold in his camp and tell him about the strange dream\tGrimbold is in his camp, north of your bedroll. You have had a most peculiar dream, if dream it was, and you should tell Grimbold of it.\n",
[2187]="7000119C\n1\tTalk to Corunir\tCorunir is at Aughaire, a Hillman-village in Angmar, somewhere north of Ram Dúath. Daervunn besought you to pass north through Ram Dúath and seek out the Ranger Corunir, who dwells now among the Hillmen of Angmar.\n",
[2188]="700452AB\n1\tTalk to Guthláf and bolster his courage\tGuthláf is near Théoden, his liege, on the Field of Onslaught. Théoden has asked you to stay near to his banner-bearer Guthláf and bolster his courage.\n2\tTalk to Guthláf and charge with him into battle once again\tGuthláf is on the Field of Onslaught, readying to follow his lord once more into the fray.\n3\tTalk to Gléowine at Kings' End\tGléowine is at Kings' End, near the corpse of the fell-beast.\n",
[2189]="7002BFB5\n1\tTalk to Wilfrith\tWilfrith is in Forthbrond, to the west of Grimbold's Camp. Grimbold thinks you should travel to Forthbrond and speak with Wilfrith for information about tracking down Wadu's Ghost in the Gap of Rohan.\n2\tDefeat Wargs at Âthdâr ([see journal]/4)\tWilfrith heard the sound of swords clashing from the direction of the Warg-warrens of Âthdâr, west of Forthbrond. He wants you to defeat Wargs there while you search for Nona. Wilfrith thinks you might be able to learn news of Nona by travelling to the Warg-warrens of Âthdâr.\n3\tDefeat Wargs at Âthdâr (3/4)\tWilfrith heard the sound of swords clashing from the direction of the Warg-warrens of Âthdâr, west of Forthbrond. He wants you to defeat Wargs there while you search for Nona. Wilfrith thinks you might be able to learn news of Nona by travelling to the Warg-warrens of Âthdâr.\n4\tInvestigate the flash of gold on the western side of Âthdâr\tYou caught a glimpse of gold from the western side of the Warg-warrens of Âthdâr. You should investigate the golden glimpse you saw at Âthdâr.\n5\tInvestigate the glint of gold to the west of Âthdâr\tYou have spied another glint of gold to the west of Âthdâr, where two trails meet. A member of the Draig-lûth killed by a sword-stroke clutched gold pieces in his hand. What does it mean?\n6\tInvestigate the glint of gold even further to the west\tYou have spied another glint of gold to the west of the small pile of gold you discovered. Someone has been leaving small piles of gold pieces in the Gap of Rohan. Is it Nona?\n7\tInvestigate the glint of gold to the south-west\tYou have spotted another glint of gold to the south-west of the gold coins you discovered, to the west of Cuvnerth. You are following a trail of gold pieces through the Gap of Rohan. Does this trail near its end?\n8\tTalk to Nona west of Cuvnerth, in the Gap of Rohan\tYou have found Nona in the Gap of Rohan, west of Cuvnerth. You should tell Nona about the troubling dream.\n",
[2190]="7002BFB8\n1\tMeet Nona at the front gate of Lhanuch, in Enedwaith\tThe front gate of Lhanuch is in Nan Laeglin, in Enedwaith, north of Dunland. Nona has agreed to come with you to Lothlórien seeking the meaning behind your dream, but first she wants to stop by the front gate of her home of Lhanuch to bid farewell to her father Suvulch.\n2\tTalk to Nona at the front gate of Lhanuch, in Enedwaith\tNona is at the front gate of the village of Lhanuch, in Enedwaith. Nona is waiting to speak with you in front of the gate of Lhanuch.\n3\tFind and talk to Suvulch at the Pool of the King, if he is there\tNona thinks Suvulch may be at the Pool of the King, north-west of Lhanuch. Nona could not find her father anywhere within Lhanuch, and thinks he might be at the Pool of the King.\n4\tPottery shards can be found along the edges of the Pool of the King. Suvulch wants you to sift through the pottery shards for something he can give to Nona as a memento.\t\n5\tBring the shining beryl to Suvulch\tSuvulch is on the shore by the Pool of the King, in Enedwaith, north-west of the village of Lhanuch. You have found a shining beryl on the shore of the Pool of the King, and should bring it to Suvulch.\n",
[2191]="7000170E\n1\tTake a rubbing from a lesser watching-stone\tLesser watching-stones litter the landscape of western Angmar, especially near Angmarim and Hillman encampments. Corunir believes that the secret of Rammas Deluon can be revealed by investigating one of the lesser watching-stones. He has instructed you to find one of the lesser stones and take a rubbing of the runes upon it. He warned you to avoid fell and deadly watching-stones.\n2\tBring the watching-stone rubbing to Corunir\tCorunir is at the Hillman-village of Aughaire. With the rubbings Corunir required in hand, you should return to the Ranger with your report.\n",
[2192]="700452B8\n1\tTalk to Elfhelm near Kings' End\tElfhelm is very near to the corpse of the fell-beast at Kings' End. Gléowine sent you to find Elfhelm and get him to lead the Rohirrim during this critical moment in the fighting.\n2\tScout the battlefield north-east of Kings' End\030Scout the battlefield south of Kings' End\030Defeat your foes on the Pelennor during the battle (total: 12)\tThe enemy is massing to the south and to the north-east of Kings' End, and Elfhelm wanted you to scout those camps and slay any enemies you find.\n3\tTalk to Elfhelm south of Kings' End\tElfhelm fights in a small knot of soldiers near a fallen Mûmak south of Kings' End.\n4\tLearn what transpired at Kings' End\tThere was the sound of sudden commotion from the direction of Kings' End, and you should return there at once\n5\tTalk to Horn at Kings' End\tHorn is at Kings' End. You heard a loud commotion and should ask Horn what transpired to cause it.\n6\tTalk to Ingbert at Kings' End\tIngbert is at Kings' End.\n",
[2193]="7000170F\n1\tExamine Lifeless Watching-stone\tLifeless watching-stones can be found in Western Malenhad, far to the east of Aughaire. Corunir has asked you to find one of the stone-hearts the runes spoke of by searching lifeless watching-stones.\n2\tBring the cracked stone-heart to Corunir\tCorunir is at the Hillman-village of Aughaire. You should return to Corunir with the stone-heart that you discovered.\n",
[2194]="7002BFBE\n1\tTravel to Lothlórien and speak with Haldir on his flet outside the borders\tHaldir is on a flet outside Lothlórien. You should speak to Haldir to obtain permission to travel with Nona into Lothlórien.\n",
[2195]="700452B7\n1\tTalk to Forlong north of Kings' End\030Talk to Hirluin north of Kings' End\tForlong and Hirluin are north of Kings' End.\n2\tReturn to Ingbert at Kings' End\tIngbert is at Kings' End.\n3\tTalk to Ingbert and complete 'Instance: The Foe Resurgent'\tIngbert is at Kings' End, waiting to speak with you and return to battle.\n4\tTalk to Éomer at Riders' Stand\tÉomer and his men have been surrounded on a hillock and cut off from the rest of the defenders.\n5\tStudy Dúnhere for signs of life at Riders' Stand\tDúnhere was felled by an arrow at Riders' Stand, and Éomer begged you to check for signs of life in his fallen friend.\n6\tTalk to Éomer at Riders' Stand\tÉomer is at Riders' Stand.\n7\tFind Gondorian soldiers north of Éomer at Riders' Stand\tÉomer sent you to help Gondorian soldiers atop the hillock at Riders' Stand.\n8\tTalk to Forlong at Riders' Stand\tForlong kneels by the body of his friend Hirluin at Riders' Stand.\n9\tSeveral approaches climb up the hill at Riders' Stand. Forlong has asked you to scout the approaches up the hill, even if you think it futile to do so.\t\n10\tTalk to Éomer on the south-western outcropping of the hillock\tÉomer has climbed a rocky outcropping on the south-western side of the hillock.\n",
[2196]="7002BFC2\n1\tTalk to Haldir and he will take you to see Galadriel\tHaldir is waiting to bring you to see Galadriel, assuming Nona will wear a blindfold. Haldir is on his flet outside Lothlórien.\n2\tTalk to Alfrohir in Thinglad\tAlfrohir is in Thinglad, along the Great River. You have been ferried across the river into Thinglad.\n",
[2197]="700452C6\n1\tLook into the distance and see what Éomer has seen\tÉomer asked you to look into the distance and see what has so disturbed him.\n2\tTalk to Éomer on the south-western outcropping of the hillock\tÉomer is on a rocky outcropping on the south-western side of the hillock at Riders' Stand.\n3\tDefeat foes on the hillock (total: 4)\tForces of the Enemy approach the hillock as you seek to master your doubt and fear.\n4\tDefeat more foes on the hillock (total: 4)\tForces of the Enemy approach the hillock as you seek to master your doubt and fear.\n5\tDefeat even more foes on the hillock (total: 4)\tForces of the Enemy approach the hillock as you seek to master your doubt and fear.\n6\tTalk to Éomer on the south-western outcropping of the hillock\tÉomer stands on the rocky outcropping on the south-western corner of the hillock, but his mood is greatly changed.\n",
[2198]="70001710\n1\tBring the stone-heart to Corunir\030Collect the stone-heart\tTath is at Tór Gailvin, north-east of Aughaire, east of the Fail-á-Khro. Corunir has sent you to Tór Gailvin to wrest a stone-heart from a sorcerer of Angmar named Tath.\n",
[2199]="7000137F\n1\tDefeat Enraged Fell Spirit\030Present the stone-heart to the ancient watching-stone\tThe ancient watching-stone is near the eastern pass of Ram Dúath, near Bail Róva, east of Aughaire. Corunir believes that the stone-heart may be able to draw forth the fell spirit from another watching-stone and has asked you to test his theory upon an ancient watching-stone which guards the passes of Ram Dúath.\n2\tTalk to Corunir\tCorunir is at the Hillman-village of Aughaire, west of Bail Róva. With the spirit of the ancient watching-stone defeated, you should return to Corunir with the news of hope.\n",
[2200]="7002C5A4\n1\tTalk to Fimloth\tHaldirith is an Elf-camp located in the northern area of Thinglad. Alfrohir has brought you from Lothlórien to Thinglad along the Great River, and thinks you should present yourself to Fimloth at Haldirith, in Thinglad.\n2\tFollow the river-bank south of Haldirith\tThe Fellowship passed south along the river, and Fimloth thinks if you seek news of your friends you should follow the river-bank south looking for signs of their passage.\n3\tFollow the river-bank further south of Haldirith\tThe Fellowship passed south along the river, and Fimloth thinks if you seek news of your friends you should follow the river-bank south looking for signs of their passage.\n4\tSearch south along the river\tYou have been following the river south in search of signs of the Fellowship's passage.\n5\tBring Orc arrow to Fimloth at Haldirith\tFimloth is at Haldirith. You should return to Fimloth at Haldirith and give her the Orc arrow and news of the slain scout you discovered.\n6\tDefeat Orcs in Thinglad (total: 8)\tOrcs can be found in great numbers throughout Thinglad. Fimloth has asked you to defeat Orcs throughout Thinglad.\n7\tTalk to Fimloth\tFimloth is at Haldirith in Thinglad. You have defeated many Orcs and should return to Fimloth at Haldirith in Thinglad.\n8\tTalk to Nona\tNona is at Haldirith, in Thinglad. Nona wishes to speak with you.\n",
[2201]="700452CC\n1\tUse the swift horse by the south-west out-cropping of Riders' Stand to travel to the Ruin of Pel Dúven\tThe newly-arrived allies that sailed on the Black Ships will disembark and make for the Ruin of Pel Dúven. Éomer has directed you to use the swift horse at the base of the outcropping on the south-west side of Riders' Stand to ride to meet the new arrivals.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn at the Ruin of Pel Dúven\tAragorn and the Grey Company have come to the Ruin of Pel Dúven.\n3\tTalk to Halbarad at the Ruin of Pel Dúven\tHalbarad is at the Ruin of Pel Dúven.\n4\tHalbarad has told you that some of the bodies littering the Ruin of Pel Dúven are not truly dead, and wants you to examine them for would-be ambushers feigning death.\t\n5\tTalk to Radanir on the eastern side of the Ruin of Pel Dúven\tRadanir is injured on the eastern side of the Ruin of Pel Dúven.\n6\tYou heard a great commotion coming from the north-west side of the Ruin of Pel Dúven, and should investigate.\t\n7\tTalk to Corunir at the Ruin of Pel Dúven\tCorunir has become very angry about something, and threatens a Gondorian man at the Ruin of Pel Dúven. Halbarad has asked you to help him calm down Corunir before the Ranger does something he will regret.\n8\tTalk to Amegil at the Ruin of Pel Dúven\tAmegil is frightened, but you would hear what he has said that has so enraged Corunir.\n9\tTalk to Amegil at the Ruin of Pel Dúven\tAmegil has cast off his fright, and he speaks now with prideful anger.\n10\tTalk to Corunir at the Ruin of Pel Dúven\tCorunir is beside himself with anger at the Ruin of Pel Dúven.\n",
[2202]="700452D4\n1\tTalk to Corunir in the Ruin of Pel Dúven and go in search of Golodir\tCorunir is in the north-west area of the Ruin of Pel Dúven.\n2\tReturn to the Rangers in the Ruin of Pel Dúven\tThe Rangers gather in the Ruin of Pel Dúven to mourn Golodir.\n3\tTalk to Halbarad in the Ruin of Pel Dúven\tThe Rangers gather in the Ruin of Pel Dúven to mourn Golodir.\n4\tTalk to Aragorn in the Ruin of Pel Dúven\tThe Rangers gather in the Ruin of Pel Dúven to mourn Golodir.\n5\tTalk to Corunir in the Ruin of Pel Dúven\tThe Rangers gather in the Ruin of Pel Dúven to mourn Golodir.\n",
[2203]="700011C5\n1\tSearch for survivors from Golodir's band\tRammas Deluon lies far to the east of Aughaire in Malenhad. Corunir suggested you look for a dwarf encampment in the south past the Rammas Deluon. Corunir bade you pass through Rammas Deluon, for you no longer have cause to fear the deadly stones. He hopes that you may find a remnant of the force Golodir led through the stones somewhere on the other side.\n",
[2204]="7002C5B1\n1\tTalk to Afic\tStangard is in Eorlsmead, south of Thinglad. You have decided to travel with Nona to the Rohirrim village of Stangard, in order to learn what you can of the situation alongside the river and the meaning behind your dream.\n2\tTalk to Nona\tNona is outside the gate of Stangard, in Eorlsmead. Afic refuses to allow Nona to enter Stangard before you show her sword to a man called Horn, near the top of the village.\n3\tCollect Nona's sword from the bag containing her possessions\tNona's sword is packed within her belongings near the entrance to Stangard. Nona has given you permission to show her sword to Horn, as long as you let no one touch it.\n4\tTalk to Horn\tHorn can be found atop the village of Stangard, in Eorlsmead. Nona has given you her sword to show to Horn, with the instruction that no one but you is to handle it.\n5\tTalk to Nona\tNona is at the gate of Stangard. Horn was very interested in Nona's sword, and wants you to return it to her before meeting him outside the town.\n",
[2205]="700452D3\n1\tTalk to Corunir in the Ruin of Pel Dúven and take the field\tCorunir is in the Ruin of Pel Dúven, waiting to take the field with you in memory of Golodir.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn at the Threshold of the City\tAragorn is at the Threshold of the City.\n",
[2206]="7002C5E5\n1\tTalk to Horn\tHorn is waiting for you by the Cuthstan in the Wailing Hills, west of Stangard. The Rohirrim man Horn wants to speak with you at the Cuthstan about something.\n2\tDefeat Prowling Orc\030Use Large Stone\tA stone you can hide behind is near the Cuthstan, just to the east of Horn. Horn hears someone approaching, and he wants you to hide behind a stone to get the drop on the newcomer if it be a foe.\n3\tTalk to Horn\tHorn is waiting for you by the Cuthstan, among the Wailing Hills, west of Stangard. You have dealt with an Orc interloper, and should speak now to Horn.\n4\tDefeat Searching Orc\030Use Large Stone\tAnother stone you can hide behind is near the Cuthstan, east of Horn. Horn hears someone approaching, and he wants you to hide behind a stone to get the drop on the newcomer if it be a foe.\n5\tTalk to Horn\tHorn is waiting for you by the Cuthstan, among the Wailing Hills, west of Stangard. You have dealt with another Orc interloper, and should speak now to Horn.\n6\tTalk to Horn\tHorn is waiting for you in the village of Stangard, in Eorlsmead. You have spoken with Horn at the Cuthstan, and he wants to speak with you some more back in Stangard.\n",
[2207]="7002C5F0\n1\tTalk to Cerdic\tCerdic is at the watch-post on the road into Parth Celebrant. Horn has given you a map of notable sites at the Battle of the Field of Celebrant to show to Cerdic.\n2\tSift through debris by the base of the crumbled pillar\030Sift through debris at the arrow-riddled patch of ground\030Sift through debris beside the bridge to Ost Celebrant\tCerdic has marked three locations in Parth Celebrant on your map: the crumbled base of a pillar, an arrow-riddled patch of ground, and the river-bank by one of the bridges to Ost Celebrant. The first two sites are on the Field of Celebrant directly south of Cerdic, and the third site is to the south-east, alongside the river. Cerdic and Horn want you to search significant locations from the Battle of the Field of Celebrant.\n3\tBring the battlefield map and the heirloom to Cerdic\tCerdic is at the watch-post on the road as it enters Parth Celebrant from Eorlsmead. You have found a bronze-worked heirloom at one of the sites of the battle with the Easterlings five hundred years ago, and should show it to Cerdic.\n4\tTalk to Edbrit at Aculf's Camp in the Rushgore\tEdbrit is in the Rushgore at Aculf's Camp, south-east of Cerdic on the very edge of the swamp. While you were searching the battlefield of Parth Celebrant, Cerdic received word from Edbrit in the Rushgore about strange happenings.\n",
[2208]="700452D2\n1\tTalk to Elfhelm\tSurvivors of a long and weary day have come to the Threshold of the City, nursing their wounds and mourning their dead.\n2\tTalk to Gléowine\tSurvivors of a long and weary day have come to the Threshold of the City, nursing their wounds and mourning their dead.\n3\tTalk to Imrahil\030Talk to Éomer\030Talk to Gimli\030Talk to Sakalbâr\030Talk to Duinhir\tSurvivors of a long and weary day have come to the Threshold of the City, nursing their wounds and mourning their dead.\n4\tTalk to Aragorn at the Threshold of the City\tAragorn is at the Threshold of the City.\n",
})
